A||N||12||kornholio||How many amps does my alternator put out?||||1||
Z||000000||kornholio||02-11-2001||07:03 PM||||Which alternator do I need?  I have an 86 V6 and I think my alternator is almost finished.  Do I need a 94 amp or a 66 amp alternator?  Does it matter?  I can get either one for the same price.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||02-11-2001||08:08 PM||||read the code on front compartmemt sticker<BR>k60= 100 amp<BR>k99= 85 amp<BR>k81= 66amp<BR>  ray||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||02-11-2001||08:30 PM||||That could be a problem...there is no sticker anywhere inside the front compartment.  Is there another way to tell?  I was just thinking the more amps the alternator puts out, the better.  Am I wrong?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||02-11-2001||08:46 PM|||| top of inner wheel well next to master cyl.<BR>3"*5" white sticker has all your codes. if air cond use biger amp one .||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-11-2001||10:18 PM||||94 amp for an '85 GT (V6) with A/C.  I'll bet yours is the same.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||02-11-2001||10:40 PM||||is it bad to have a higher powered alternator? i bought a 100-amp one recently. haven't put it in yet though.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||02-11-2001||11:20 PM||||Usually a higher output will live a happier life and last longer because it is not running at its full capacity all the time. I try to buy the highest output that will fit so when I am idling with all accessories running the voltage will not dip too low.<P>------------------<BR>Just because you can't do it doesn't mean it can't be done.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||02-12-2001||02:14 AM||||RPO code K22 is for the 94 amp alt.  Get the 94 amp.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||02-12-2001||05:32 PM||||while were talkin alternators here, whats the output on your cars gauge? Mine has alway run fine, same battery for 3 years , 40K and its always just been to the left of the red. How come it doesnt stay in center? every other car ive owned stayed just slightly to right of center. Just wondered if thats normal for Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ben84||02-12-2001||07:17 PM||||I have the same problem...No compartment sticker to determine the alternator for my 84 2m4.... So please drop a little wisdom reply...Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||02-12-2001||07:47 PM||||When you fill in all the questions at the parts store.. year, engine, AC, etc, they usually give you the right one. If you have power everything or a big aftermarket audio rig get the 90-100 amp ones. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||kornholio||02-12-2001||09:02 PM||||Is there a downside to getting an alternator with a higher amperage rating?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||02-12-2001||11:50 PM||||Higher Amp alternators usually cost a little more but that's the only downside.  Unless you have a totally stripped down car with no A/C, no power anything you should get the 94 amp.  If you have the bare-bones car than the 66 amp will work.  ||||reg||1
